{
  "name": "Sort website leads by urgency with OpenAI and alert on urgent jobs",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "4cbaa309-9a45-409e-bbef-fd5b06279e65",
      "name": "Overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -560,
        -260
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Sort website leads by urgency and alert on the urgent ones\n\n### How it works\nBuilt for local trades (plumbing, HVAC, roofing, pool, lawn). A website form posts each new lead to the Webhook. OpenAI reads the request and labels it HOT, WARM or COLD, where HOT means something urgent like a leak, no AC or an open roof. Every lead is logged to a Google Sheet. HOT leads also send you an email right away so a burst pipe never waits behind a gutter quote. If the AI call fails, the lead is still logged with score COLD so nothing is lost.\n\n### Setup\n1. Make a Google Sheet with a tab named `CRM` and columns: id, date, name, email, phone, service, source, score, status, notes.\n2. In **Log Lead to Sheet**, pick your Google Sheets credential and replace REPLACE_WITH_SPREADSHEET_ID with your sheet ID.\n3. In **Score Lead Urgency**, pick your OpenAI credential. OpenAI bills per use; set a spending limit.\n4. In **Edit These Settings**, set your email and trade.\n5. In **Email Owner About Urgent Lead**, pick your Gmail credential.\n6. Point your form at the production webhook URL. It expects JSON: name, email, phone, service, message.\n\n### Customization\nChange what counts as HOT in the prompt. Swap the email for a Slack or Telegram node.",
        "width": 420,
        "height": 760
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "dbe5b67a-9ff0-41d8-8343-fc8b5a198b0f",
